{:edb/db-before-t 1988 :edb/db-after-t 1989 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535301 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:39:17.131Z" 13194139535301 true] [17592186133473 1100 "Consider ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/ba3f1852b12b6f4a246a855c88c9b867b7e750c6dddf350cab0324629fc047c4.png) and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." 13194139535301 true] [17592186133473 1100 "Consider $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$.\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A$, is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." 13194139535301 false] [17592186133473 1145 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} + 7R_{3} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary\nrow operation\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+7R_3\n$$\n\nto $A$." 13194139535301 false] [17592186133473 1145 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation $R_2 :=R_2+7R_3$ to $A.$" 13194139535301 true] [17592186133474 1100 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$. What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" 13194139535301 false] [17592186133474 1100 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" 13194139535301 true] [17592186133474 1145 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation\n\n$$\nR_2:= R_2-2R_1\n$$\n\nto $A$.\n\nTo find $E$, we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} - 2R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139535301 false] [17592186133474 1145 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2-2R_1$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/8d015aca8950073c165d53b14f86f0e65a207438ad901ce82f85f65bb8347519.png)" 13194139535301 true] [17592186133475 1100 "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$:\n$R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad R_1:=6R_1$\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535301 false] [17592186133475 1100 "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad\n\tR_1:=6R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139535301 true] [17592186133475 1145 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid ↔R_{3}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{1}$\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1} \\mid:=6R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{2}$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A$, we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A$, we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139535301 false] [17592186133475 1145 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/375f1950c460b1f310fa279f6d7f203f88ff641000715dfaec192f47d785aa93.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/6357cc2a2526f38a0f0f7e2e7ef4ee7a1a564adfa70264028ff732f44ba7b763.png)" 13194139535301 true] [17592186133665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342666 13194139535301 true] [17592186133665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342673 13194139535301 true] [17592186133665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342749 13194139535301 true] [17592186133665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342756 13194139535301 true] [17592186133666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342680 13194139535301 true] [17592186133666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342714 13194139535301 true] [17592186133666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342728 13194139535301 true] [17592186133666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342742 13194139535301 true] [17592186133667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342687 13194139535301 true] [17592186133667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342694 13194139535301 true] [17592186133667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342701 13194139535301 true] [17592186133667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342721 13194139535301 true] [17592186133667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342735 13194139535301 true] [17592186134106 1017 #edb/ref 17592186131082 13194139535301 false] [17592186134106 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342708 13194139535301 true] [17592186134106 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535301 true] [17592186134106 1100 "Suppose that the elementary row operation $R_{2}:=R_{2} - 3R_{3}$ is applied to a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$. What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" 13194139535301 false] [17592186134106 1100 "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" 13194139535301 true] [17592186134106 1145 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139535301 true] [17592186134109 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535301 true] [17592186134109 1100 "Consider $E = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$.\n\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A$, is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." 13194139535301 false] [17592186134109 1100 "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." 13194139535301 true] [17592186134109 1145 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the second rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ to $A.$" 13194139535301 true] [17592186342666 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342667 13194139535301 true] [17592186342666 1089 "q-110458" 13194139535301 true] [17592186342666 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535301 true] [17592186342666 1100 "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." 13194139535301 true] [17592186342666 1113 #uuid "9b58aedf-3f0d-5c92-904c-dcfbb7d809b6" 13194139535301 true] [17592186342666 1145 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of ${I}_{3}$ by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342668 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342669 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342670 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342671 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342672 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1041 "selection" 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342670 13194139535301 true] [17592186342667 1110 #uuid "ea289ba4-c39d-5